.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-check 1  "ngx-check " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-check \- Check every site for monitoring/cron: down sites, expired or expiring certificates, renewal problems
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-check\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check every site for monitoring/cron: down sites, expired or expiring certificates, renewal problems
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No output, only the exit status
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
Exit status: 0 all good, 1 warnings, 2 a site is down or a certificate expired/missing.

Examples:
  ngx check
  ngx check \-\-json
  # /etc/cron.d/ngx\-check: mail the report when something is wrong (needs a working `mail`)
  MAILTO=you@example.com
  0 8 * * * root ngx check \-q || ngx check
